<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Purandara Dasa</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">c. 1484–<a href="/years/1564">1564</a></span> · <a href="/centuries/16th-century">16th century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Purandara <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/dasa">Dasa</a> was a <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/kannada">Kannada</a> poet-saint and composer of the Haridasa devotional movement who lived in the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/vijayanagara-empire">Vijayanagara Empire</a>. A wealthy merchant before he gave away his property, he composed thousands of devotional songs to <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/vishnu">Vishnu</a>. He systematised the teaching of Carnatic music, devising graded exercises still used by beginners, and is traditionally called the father of Carnatic music.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/purandara-dasa.jpg" alt="Purandara Dasa" width="230" height="300" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Music and dance on stamps · CC BY-SA 4.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:481_Purandardasa.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
<section class="enc-quotes"><h2 class="enc-section-title">Across the Institute</h2><ul><li><blockquote>The composer <b>Purandara Dasa</b>, traditionally regarded as the father of Carnatic music, lived and worked within the empire.</blockquote><a href="/empire/vijayanagara-empire">Vijayanagara Empire · Global &amp; Regional Impact</a></li><li><blockquote>In the Vijayanagara Empire the Haridasas, among them <b>Purandara Dasa</b>, sang to Vishnu in Kannada.</blockquote><a href="/movement/bhakti-movement">Bhakti movement · Course of Events</a></li></ul></section>
<section class="enc-where enc-born"><h2 class="enc-section-title">Born and died</h2><p class="enc-born-p">Born in Thirthahalli, in what is now <a href="/countries/india">India</a>. Died in Hampi, in what is now <a href="/countries/india">India</a>. <span class="enc-born-src">Places as Wikidata records them.</span></p><figure class="st-locator enc-loc"><a href="/atlas?at=13.7,75.23&amp;year=1536" aria-label="Thirthahalli on the atlas"><svg class="map map-loc" viewBox="6611 1653 900 540" role="img" aria-label="Map: the birthplace of Purandara Dasa"><image href="/maps/world.svg" x="0" y="0" width="10000" height="4393"/><path class="map-dot-halo" d="M7061 1923h0"/><path class="map-dot-me" d="M7061 1923h0"/></svg></a><figcaption>The dot marks the birthplace. <a href="/atlas?at=13.7,75.23&amp;year=1536">What was here in 1536? &rarr;</a></figcaption></figure></section>
